{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat tests/helpers.ts && cat README.md && cat src/server.ts && node --version && npm --version && rg --files -g AGENTS.md /private/tmp/claude-502 2>/dev/null'","aggregated_output":"import type { AddressInfo } from \"node:net\";\nimport { createApp } from \"../src/app.ts\";\nimport { BookStore, type NewBook } from \"../src/store.ts\";\n\n/** Start the app on a free port with these books; returns its base URL and a stop function. */\nexport async function serve(books: NewBook[] = []): Promise<{ url: string; stop: () => void }> {\n  const server = createApp(new BookStore(books)).listen(0);\n  await new Promise((resolve) => server.once(\"listening\", resolve));\n  const { port } = server.address() as AddressInfo;\n  return { url: `http://127.0.0.1:${port}`, stop: () => server.close() };\n}\n\nexport async function send(url: string, method: string, body?: unknown) {\n  const response = await fetch(url, {\n    method,\n    headers: body === undefined ? {} : { \"content-type\": \"application/json\" },\n    body: body === undefined ? undefined : JSON.stringify(body),\n  });\n  return { status: response.status, body: await response.json() };\n}\n# library-api\n\nA small HTTP API for a lending library, on Express 5. Data is kept in memory.\n\n```bash\nnpm install\nPORT=3000 npm start\nnpm test\n```\n\n| Method and path | What it does |\n|-----------------|--------------|\n| `GET /books` | every book, by id |\n| `GET /books/:id` | one book, or 404 |\n| `POST /books` | add a book: JSON `{\"title\": \"...\", \"author\": \"...\"}`; 201 with the book, 400 on bad input |\n| `GET /health` | `{\"status\": \"ok\"}` |\n\nA book is `{\"id\": 1, \"title\": \"...\", \"author\": \"...\"}`. Errors are JSON `{\"error\": \"...\"}`.\n`createApp(store)` in `src/app.ts` builds the application (the tests use it with a fresh store).\nimport { createApp } from \"./app.ts\";\nimport { BookStore } from \"./store.ts\";\n\nconst port = Number(process.env.PORT ?? 3000);\nconst store = new BookStore([\n  { title: \"The Left Hand of Darkness\", author: \"Ursula K. Le Guin\" },\n  { title: \"Kindred\", author: \"Octavia E. Butler\" },\n]);\ncreateApp(store).listen(port, () => {\n  console.log(`library-api listening on http://127.0.0.1:${port}`);\n});\nv24.14.1\n11.11.0\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
